From f545c808204f7236bcc480c87da315add3539cdf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Indan Zupancic <indan@nul.nu>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:39:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] SMP: backport upstream IPI bugfixes and improvements

Squash seL4/seL4#1849 at 59c2595a24cc64f1c291634ed7c4e3e912173d1b.
Upstream-PR: https://github.com/seL4/seL4/pull/1849
Upstream-base: c98d70adf15e8be7d3b99085c28d057069ba7155

Includes all eight PR commits, including the GenMC lock and IPI models:
  55899850c Arm, SMP: implement arch_pause
  972f55404 SMP: Add clh_lock_acquire_slowpath
  ee74342fe SMP: Minor Cleanup
  25b5acc6c SMP: IPI bugfixes and improvements
  e3625273d SMP: Make locking code pass GenMC model checking
  5293f03ab SMP: Add GenMC big kernel lock test
  e39343e28 SMP: Remove IPI_MEM_BARRIER
  59c2595a2 SMP: Add GenMC test for IPI / remote core calls

Blocking IPIs run only while waiting for the global kernel lock. Stalls
that race a syscall or fault refuse the operation so its caller retries;
IRQ-path stalls save live x86 FS/GS before switching to the idle thread.
The new call counter and pending-call ordering supersede l4h patches
0005 and 0010.

Backport adaptations for l4h's extensions:
- Preserve patch 0012's stale-timer fast return for native threads, with
  explicit lock ownership rather than clh_is_self_in_queue(). VM returns
  use the locked path and retain VCPU/notification/exit preparation.
- Retain the EPT invalidation remote-call case from patch 0039.
- Use switchLocalFpuOwner() for patch 0002's current-thread FPU reload;
  upstream removed the redundant switchFpuOwner() wrapper.
- Stall both affected TCBs before VCPU rebinding and stall the bound TCB
  before final VCPU deletion, propagating EXCEPTION_PREEMPTED without
  changing bindings if either stall refuses. TCB deletion already uses
  upstream's retry path. Remove the now redundant inner dissociation stall.

Co-authored-by: l4h <z@univalence.me>
